{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moshe: Is HaShem's hand shortened?</b> That is, just as it is in My power to provide, so is it in My power to hold their hands, so that My words will be fulfilled — as it is said: ״ויטוש על המחנה״ etc., ״וכאמתים על פני הארץ״ — from a height, such that they did not need even to extend a hand. Another interpretation: ״הצאן ובקר״ etc. — surely Moshe knew that there is power in the hand of the Holy One, blessed be He, to provide. Rather, this is what it says: You forbade them the meat of craving except through the offering of a sacrifice at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting, and there are only three kohanim here — Aharon and his sons — and if so, the surplus would come into the status of notar, for they would not be able to eat it all. ״If all the fish of the sea were gathered for them״ — and found for them conveniently, that is, if they had asked for fish and you had provided them, it would be fine, for there is no sacrifice involved; but meat that you said to give them, which implies from sheep and cattle, is difficult, because they must make a sacrifice from them. ״And HaShem said to Moshe: Is HaShem's hand shortened? You will now see״ — that I will give them meat and they will not need a sacrifice, and this is the quail, from which no sacrifice is brought."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:14.870380465Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}